# Crypto Screener V5 ONE TICK loop — self-paced, read roadmap and execute first unchecked task
# Run: claude "/loop $(tail -1 CRYPTO_LOOP_V5.sh)"
# Or paste the last line into claude with /loop

Read docs/CRYPTO_V5_ONE_TICK_ROADMAP.md and follow its doctrine and hard rules exactly. Do only the first unchecked [ ] task. Doctrine recap: DESIGN FREEZE — zero visual redesign, Markets.tsx table and AssetInfoPanel keep their exact look, only the numbers' source changes. ONE SOURCE RULE: a crypto number rendered in two places must be read from the same client store field — never two fetches for one fact. Truth rules verbatim from V3/V4: price gate (venue vs CG base 3%, stables 1%), CG-id joins where ids exist, honest '—' beats plausible numbers, no zeros-as-data. Standing constraints: NO new serverless files (?view= branches in api/crypto/markets.ts only), vercel.json keeps "regions":["fra1"], keyless APIs only (public WebSocket streams are keyless — native WebSocket, no new npm deps), additive payloads. Audit tooling: apps/market-ui/scripts/audit_crypto_coverage.mjs must stay green (spot 100/100, MISMATCH 0) after every task — rerun and paste REAL numbers into the Progress log. Verify per task: market-ui typecheck 0 + vercel --prod (from repo root — apps/market-ui path breaks project link) + prod curl/browser evidence with real numbers. Flip the task to [x], append one Progress-log line, commit on roadmap/world-class (git commit -F file if the message has quotes — rtk mangles them). PERSISTENCE: never end the loop because of a usage/rate limit, 429, or overloaded error — on any such error stop consuming tokens, ScheduleWakeup at 3600s with this exact /loop prompt, and on wake re-read the ledger and resume the same task from its last verified step (ledger + Progress log + CRYPTO_COVERAGE_AUDIT.md are recovery state; log partial progress BEFORE long/risky operations); chain hourly wakeups as needed. Only stop for: no [ ] remaining, or a task blocked on something only the user can provide — then say exactly what's needed and still ScheduleWakeup (3600s) so the loop resumes if supplied.
